The "orders" section in this TG specifies the sequence in which tasks should be executed under certain conditions. However, given that all tasks depend on both CarXSpeedCalculation and CarYSpeedCalculation, the current order setup is indeed redundant because each task can logically be executed independently after their respective inputs are calculated.

To improve clarity and ensure correct execution without redundancy, the "orders" section could be simplified or removed if the dependencies naturally follow from the task definitions. In this case, since both SpeedDifferenceCalculation tasks depend on CarXSpeedCalculation and CarYSpeedCalculation, they can be executed in any order after those two tasks are completed.

A more streamlined TG might look like this:

```json
{
    "owner_agent": "CalcDifEq",
    "tasks": {
        "CarXSpeedCalculation": "Calculate the speed of car X using distance and time given",
        "CarYSpeedCalculation": "Calculate the speed of car Y using distance and time given",
        "SpeedDifferenceCalculation": "Find the difference in speeds between car X and car Y"
    },
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": ["CarXSpeedCalculation", "CarYSpeedCalculation"],
            "to": "SpeedDifferenceCalculation"
        }
    ],
    "refused": false,
    "answer": null
}
```

This structure ensures that SpeedDifferenceCalculation can only proceed once both CarXSpeedCalculation and CarYSpeedCalculation have succeeded, without the redundancy of specifying separate orders for each task.
